@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@* FR-79 / FR-80: AuthorizeRouteView's NotAuthorized branch, which exists to send the caller
   somewhere rather than to say anything.

   It renders nothing on purpose - a page of prose explaining that a redirect is about to happen is
   a second thing to read before being redirected - and it renders nothing on BOTH paths, which is
   the part that matters: with prerendering off (AD-14) and no route view in this fragment, the
   protected component's markup cannot reach the response whichever way the decision goes.

   Which way it goes is AuthFailureRoute's, not this component's: a caller who is already signed in
   and still refused must not be told to sign in again. *@

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The circuit's authentication state, cascaded by <c>AddCascadingAuthenticationState</c>. Read
    /// through the cascade rather than through ICurrentUser because this component runs inside the
    /// route view, where the cascade is the framework's own answer to the same question.
    /// </summary>
    [CascadingParameter]
    private Task<AuthenticationState>? AuthenticationState { get; set; }

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        var isAuthenticated = AuthenticationState is not null
            && (await AuthenticationState).User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true;

        Navigation.NavigateTo(AuthFailureRoute.For(isAuthenticated));
    }
}
